\frametitle{Examples}
The natural numbers type is generated by the constructors:
  \begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathsf{zero} : \N$
    \item $\mathsf{succ} : \N \to \N$
  \end{itemize}
  To prove a property $E : \N \to \U$ it suffices to prove $E(\mathsf{zero})$, and for all $n : \N$ that $E(n) \to E(\mathsf{succ}(n))$.
